      <bpmn:userTask id="W4997_Task4" name="Define the referral economics: the referral-fee/commission model (flat per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Define the referral economics: the referral-fee/commission model (flat per lead, % of project value, % of materials sold, or marketplace transaction fee), the free-vs-charge thresholds, the B2B/contract treatment (VS-11), and the tax (BIR VAT/EWT on installer fees links VS-79)
Responsible (R): Finance / Network Manager / Legal / Tax
Accountable (A): CFO / COO
Duration: Per policy</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4997_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4997_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4997_Task5" name="Calculate &amp; settle: compute the referral fee/commission per completed project…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Calculate &amp; settle: compute the referral fee/commission per completed project (W4998), invoice/collect from the installer (or deduct from marketplace settlement), issue BIR-compliant billing (links VS-79), and reconcile to finance (VS-17/VS-16)
Responsible (R): Finance / Marketplace / Tax
Accountable (A): Finance Lead
Duration: Per project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4997_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4997_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4997_Task6" name="Govern &amp; audit: monitor fee leakage/revenue assurance (links VS-118)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govern &amp; audit: monitor fee leakage/revenue assurance (links VS-118), disputes/installer pushback, audit the settlement (VS-21), and refine the economics (W4985)
Responsible (R): Finance / Audit / Network Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4997_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4997_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
