    <bpmn:process id="W_W5000" name="W5000. Lost/Declined Lead Recovery, Alternate Referral &amp; Demand Capture" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Lead declined/unaccepted (W4994); quote lost (W4995); installer unavailable
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: ~500–1,000 lost/declined leads per month across the network
Owner: Pro-Referral Network Manager / CX (VS-13)
Participants: CX (VS-13), Marketplace (VS-95), Analytics (VS-28), Services (VS-12), Installer
Source: workflow W5000 — Lost/Declined Lead Recovery, Alternate Referral &amp; Demand Capture</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5000_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5000_Lane1" name="Marketplace">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5000_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5000_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5000_Lane2" name="CX">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5000_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5000_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5000_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5000_Start4" name="Lead declined/unaccepted (W4994); quote lost (W4995); installer unavailable">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5000_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5000_Task5" name="Detect lost/declined leads: monitor unaccepted leads (W4994), lost quotes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Detect lost/declined leads: monitor unaccepted leads (W4994), lost quotes (W4995), and abandoned requests; flag for recovery within the response SLA
Responsible (R): Marketplace / Analytics / CX
Accountable (A): Network Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5000_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5000_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5000_Task6" name="Recover via alternate referral: re-route to alternate installers (W4994), offer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Recover via alternate referral: re-route to alternate installers (W4994), offer BuildRight&#x27;s own crews (VS-12) where available, or recommend delivery/alternatives (VS-06/VS-143); keep the customer engaged
Responsible (R): CX / Marketplace / Services
Accountable (A): Network Manager
Duration: Per lead</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5000_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5000_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5000_Task7" name="Capture demand &amp; learn: even if referral fails, capture the project demand…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Capture demand &amp; learn: even if referral fails, capture the project demand (materials sale, financing VS-154, design VS-66), analyze loss reasons (coverage W4991, pricing, capacity), and feed improvement
Responsible (R): CX / Analytics / Network Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5000_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5000_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5000_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5000_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5000_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-747 (ensure controlled execution — Pro-Referral Matchmaking, Project Routing &amp; Lead Management (PA-172.2).) | - CTL-747: lost leads detected within SLA; alternate referral offered; demand captured; loss reasons analyzed
Owner: Pro-Referral Network Manager / CX (VS-13)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5000_Assoc10" sourceRef="W5000_Annotation9" targetRef="W5000_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5000_Flow11" sourceRef="W5000_Start4" targetRef="W5000_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5000_Flow12" sourceRef="W5000_Task5" targetRef="W5000_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5000_Flow13" sourceRef="W5000_Task6" targetRef="W5000_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5000_Flow14" sourceRef="W5000_Task7" targetRef="W5000_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
